                "steps": [
                    {
                        "step": "pH 7.2"
                    },
                    {
                        "step": "Prepare the medium without the Na2S, Na2CO3, NaHCO3, L-cysteine and substrate. Boil the medium and cool under a stream of nitrogen. Add the Na2CO3 and NaHCO3 . Adjust the pH to 7.2. If chitin is used as the substrate it must be added before autoclaving. Autoclave the medium and add the Na2S (from a sterile, neutralized stock solution prepared under nitrogen), L-cysteine (from a stock solution prepared under nitrogen), and the glucose or N-acetylglucosamine (if used as substrate) from sterile stock solution prepared under nitrogen. Check the final pH."
                    }
                ],
